            :untruncated? true}

 :stages
 [{:stage :commissioned :verdict :operator-turn
   :turn "claude-2 wrote the commission by hand (runs/PA11z-exemplar/commission-prompt.md): the target patterns, the evidence standard, the refusal shape, the do-not-commit boundary. Nothing generated or recorded any of it."
   :finding "WORSE THAN ABSENT -- A SILENT NO-OP. The bell API ACCEPTS a `mission-id` field and returns accepted:true; I sent :mission-id \"PA11z-library-annotator-exemplar\". That string appears NOWHERE afterwards: not on the job record, and not on the live agent record while it was actively invoking. It is threaded into the invoke call (transport/http.clj:4284, agency/registry.clj:1723) but never persisted -- the job record template at transport/http.clj:1305-1315 has no mission-id field at all. So a dispatch cannot be traced back to what it was commissioned for."
   :why-this-is-the-dangerous-kind "A missing feature is visible. A field that is accepted and discarded invites the belief that commission identity IS recorded, and nothing refuses to tell you otherwise."
   :evidence ["dispatch-job-record.json (search for the mission-id string: absent)"
              "futon3c/src/futon3c/transport/http.clj:1305-1315 (job record template)"
              "futon3c/src/futon3c/transport/http.clj:4284, agency/registry.clj:1723 (threaded, not stored)"]}

  {:stage :dispatched :verdict :running-code
   :evidence ["futon3c/src/futon3c/transport/http.clj:~1305-1330 -- POST /api/alpha/bell mints the job, assigns job-id, appends the `accepted` event and returns {:accepted true :state \"queued\"}."]
   :observed "accepted 15:20:49 -> running 15:20:52, job-id minted."
   :caveat "On THIS path the dispatch RECORDS; it does not refuse. The typed refusal (`social-error :invalid-receipt` when a DispatchReceipt fails its shape) lives at social/dispatch.clj:238-266, which is the coordination-message path -- NOT the bell path this dispatch took. ALIGN's distinction holds: the machinery exists, and whether it is on your path is a separate question."}

  {:stage :parked :verdict :absent
   :finding "Nothing parked this dispatch. The caller polled the job to completion instead."
   :evidence ["futon3c/src/futon3c/agency/parked_on.clj:332-395 -- park! exists and DOES refuse (throws on a non-canonical :timer-due-ms or :deadline-ms), but it is generic, carries no node link, and nothing on the bell path invokes it."]
   :note "This is ALIGN's [A16] shape seen live: a real park facility, unreached by the path that needed it."}

  {:stage :returned :verdict :running-code
   :evidence ["The job reaches a terminal state observable by the caller: state done, finished-at 2026-09-06T15:23:15.141536726Z, followed by a delivery-recorded event; delivery {:status delivered :surface bell :destination \"caller claude-2 via /api/alpha/invoke/jobs/<id>\"}."]
   :caveat "TERMINAL-CODE IS NULL EVEN ON SUCCESS. `state` carries the outcome and `terminal-code` stays nil, so a consumer that gates on a typed terminal code rather than on the state string gets nothing to gate on. Recorded, not filed as a defect -- it is the runner's shape, not this row's to change."}

  {:stage :checked :verdict :operator-turn
   :turn "claude-2 read the returned report and judged it (1 evidence-found with a verbatim quote and a syntax-matched proposed edge; 2 honest no-committed-source with two loose candidates explicitly rejected). That judgement is the only check that happened."
   :finding "NOTHING ON THIS PATH REFUSES AN UNCHECKED RETURN. The job went to `done` and delivered with no checker between the return and the caller consuming it. R16's reviewer gate (full_loop_runner.clj:2950-2968, approval requires a done review job + :approve + execution evidence) is real but belongs to the full-loop actuator, not to a bell dispatch; and the zaif-build-loop's author!=reviewer law is asserted in a comment with nothing comparing the seats (PA5z)."
   :evidence ["dispatch-job-record.json -- no check event between `done` and `delivery-recorded`"]}

  {:stage :recorded :verdict :running-code
   :evidence ["futon3c/src/futon3c/transport/http.clj:1324-1331 -- a durable coordination edge is recorded for EVERY job, keyed by job-id, with the comment stating it is deliberately not limited to wrapped social-dispatch invokes."
              "futon3c/src/futon3c/social/coordination_ledger.clj:77-82 record-invoke-edge! appends to the evidence store."]
   :caveat "BEST-EFFORT, NOT REFUSING. The call is wrapped in (try ... (catch Throwable _)) with the comment \"Never break the hot path\", so a recording failure is swallowed silently. An assurance cell whose recorder may fail without saying so is weaker than one that refuses -- worth carrying into PA6z/PA10z rather than inheriting. It also records from/to/surface/edge-id and NOT the commission, which is the :commissioned finding again from the other side."}

  {:stage :surfaced :verdict :operator-turn
   :turn "claude-2 is surfacing this dispatch by writing it into this artifact, the PA11z row, and a bell back to claude-1. Absent that turn, the dispatch completed and nobody would learn anything from it."
   :finding "NOTHING SURFACES A COMPLETED DISPATCH. futon2/src/futon2/aif/bulletin.clj contains ZERO occurrences of job/dispatch/invoke (measured: `grep -c 'job\\|dispatch\\|invoke' src/futon2/aif/bulletin.clj` -> 0, untruncated). The bulletin surfaces commits, board deltas and waits-on-joe rows read from worklists (bulletin.clj:166-198) -- all of which reach it because an agent turn wrote them there."
   :evidence ["futon2/src/futon2/aif/bulletin.clj:166-198 (what it does read)"
              "grep count 0 for job/dispatch/invoke in that file"]}]

